.TH bhtune-template-import 1  "bhtune-template-import "
.SH NAME
bhtune\-template\-import \- Import a template from a file. Accepts either a single template as JSON (see `template export`\*(Aqs default output shape) or a multi\-template TOML catalog (the same `[[template]]` array\-of\-tables shape as the embedded/user catalog, see `template export \-\-format toml`) \-\- the format is auto\-detected from the file\*(Aqs content, not its extension. A JSON single\-template import is rejected outright if a template with that name already exists; a TOML catalog import instead skips (and reports) any template whose name already exists, so re\-importing an updated community catalog only adds what\*(Aqs new
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbhtune\-template\-import\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import a template from a file. Accepts either a single template as JSON (see `template export`\*(Aqs default output shape) or a multi\-template TOML catalog (the same `[[template]]` array\-of\-tables shape as the embedded/user catalog, see `template export \-\-format toml`) \-\- the format is auto\-detected from the file\*(Aqs content, not its extension. A JSON single\-template import is rejected outright if a template with that name already exists; a TOML catalog import instead skips (and reports) any template whose name already exists, so re\-importing an updated community catalog only adds what\*(Aqs new
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>

